  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A current $I=I_{0} e^{-\\lambda t}$ is flowing in a circuit consisting of a parallel combination of resistance $R$ and capacitance $C$. The total charge over the entire pulse period is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "40rAc",
      "text": "$\\frac{I_{0}}{\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CP0EE",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 I_{0}}{\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sUycl",
      "text": "$I_{0} \\lambda$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BHe62",
      "text": "$e^{I_{0}\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The current $1=1_{0} e^{-x}$ is of exponential nature.\r\n$I=\\frac{d Q}{d t}=I_{0} e^{-\\lambda t}$\r\n$d Q=I_{0} e^{-\\lambda t} d t$\r\n$\\int_{0}^{Q} d Q=I_{0} \\int_{t=0}^{t=-\\infty} e^{-\\lambda t} \\cdot d t$\r\n$Q=I_{0} \\times \\frac{1}{\\lambda}=\\frac{I_{0}}{\\lambda}$",
    "image": null
  },
